# LEF layer -> QRC tech file layer, Cadence format.
#
# Both stacks report 10 routing layers, but they are not the same 10:
#   LEF : M1 M2 M3 M4 M5 M6 M7 M8 M9 Pad
#   QRC : LISD M1 M2 M3 M4 M5 M6 M7 M8 M9
# Genus paired them by position, so the last run mapped LEF M1 onto QRC
# LISD, LEF M4 onto QRC M3, LEF M6 onto QRC M5 and LEF M8 onto QRC M7
# (see the four PHYS-25 warnings in genus.log).  Every layer therefore
# picked up the R and C of the layer below it.
#
# This file forces name-based matching.  Vias are deliberately left out:
# the QRC via names are not visible from the PHYS-25 messages.  If the
# QRC layer names turn out to differ from the ones below, fix them here
# and rerun; PHYS-25 disappearing from genus.log is the pass criterion.
M1 M1 \
M2 M2 \
M3 M3 \
M4 M4 \
M5 M5 \
M6 M6 \
M7 M7 \
M8 M8 \
M9 M9
